I just completed an Archaeologist ascension (my first ever Hack/Nethack
ascension), and based on my experiences in this game I have some
thoughts and ideas... 

(1) I agree with people who say the number of items (particularly wands,
    potions and scrolls) generated in the dungeon is approaching
    out-of-control proportions.  About halfway through the game, I stupidly
    blew up my bag of holding (by the WoC ruse) containing a dozen
    spellbooks, fifteen food rations, spare rings, wands, tools; 18 blank
    scrolls and 12 potions of holy water.  Even so, I had no problem
    continuing the game and quickly had 25 new potions of holy water, 12
    blank scrolls and replacements for everything but the spellbooks.  By
    the time I took on the Wiz, I ditched ANOTHER bag of holding containing
    15 _additional_ food rations, countless potions and wands.
    Of the items I carried all the way through, I didn't need a third of them.


(2) A friend started playing a character, a Samurai, the same time I
    started my -A.  He died early in Hell, about half an hour before
    I started down.  Naturally, I ran into his bones file on Lvl 35, which
    included a +4 Tsurugi, and a +3 Mitre of Holiness he had wished for.
    So, at this point I had _three_ quest artifacts. (In addition to
    YET ANOTHER stash of potions/scrolls/wands I didn't need!)

    I'm of the opinion characters shouldn't have access to quest items
    of other classes.  Just a thought.


(3) In the above case, I would have preferred to not run into my
    friend's bones (because we were playing in the same room and I 
    knew all the stuff he had).  Also, I almost always prefer to not
    run into any of my _own_ bones files (same reason).

    I wonder if Nethack couldn't have a start-of-game time option to
    say whether or not bones levels will be generated.  For example,
    I might start a character and say (a) play with normal bones or
    (b) do not permit running into one's own bones or (c) do not
    permit running into any bones.  [ If this already exists, I apologize
    for not knowing about it ].  For me, deleting/moving bones files
    isn't a good solution since other people play on my executable.
    Likewise, a compile-time option isn't good either.


(4) When my friend's character was still alive :-), he was commenting on
    how his character was superior to mine.  At the time, I thought it 
    would be interesting to get the two characters on a level to fight it out.

    For this, how about adding an "Arena Level" to Nethack.  The Arena
    would be a level populated with various monsters and characters
    from other classes (Roman Coliseum-style).  They're would be a
    grandstand (with lots of picture-taking Tourists! (re a previous
    post)) and an area for fighting, maybe a maze with walls, water,
    lava.  Arriving on this level, a character could challenge others  
    to fights for money (no Exp Pts gained) or wager on other fights.

    The other option on the Arena level would be to "program in" an
    opponent by character/inventory description (just a file).  Just
    a thought I had at the time.


Overall, I really like how the character classes are balanced in 3.1.
Even though I'm a hacker/slasher type, my two best characters have been
a Priest and this Archaeologist.  Definitely there's a big luck component
in the game, but I think that's cool.

  
bradley



